---
source: tests/cli/help_snapshots_test.rs
expression: "help_output(&[\"--help\"])"
---
Inspect and edit XMind workbooks through an agent-native CLI

Usage: xmind [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  inspect     Summarize workbook metadata, sheets, and compatibility details.
  sheets      List sheets in a workbook with ids, titles, and ordering.
  tree        Print a workbook topic tree for quick reading or scripting.
  find        Search workbook topics by title, text, or query selector.
  get         Read one topic and optionally include its descendants.
  add         Add a single topic under an existing parent topic.
  add-tree    Add a topic subtree from YAML, JSON, or Markdown input.
  set         Update topic fields such as title, notes, labels, markers, links, or images.
  delete      Delete a topic or selected descendants from a workbook.
  move        Move a topic to a different parent or sibling position.
  copy        Copy a topic subtree to another location in the workbook.
  patch       Apply a batch of structured workbook edit operations.
  diff        Show structural differences for the current workbook diff surface.
  validate    Check whether a workbook can be read and safely processed.
  export      Export workbook content to Markdown, outline, JSON, or assets.
  import      Create or update a workbook from Markdown or structured input.
  backup      Create an explicit backup copy of a workbook.
  restore     Restore workbook content from the matching backup workflow.
  completion  Generate shell completion scripts for the xmind command.
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json                       Emit a JSON command envelope
      --format <FORMAT>            Select the human or machine-readable output format [default: text] [possible values: text, json, compact-json, markdown, outline, assets]
      --fields <FIELDS>            Limit JSON output to comma-separated field paths
      --quiet                      Suppress non-essential text output
      --no-color                   Disable ANSI color in text output
      --sheet <SHEET>              Select a sheet by title
      --sheet-id <SHEET_ID>        Select a sheet by stable id
      --sheet-index <SHEET_INDEX>  Select a sheet by zero-based index
  -h, --help                       Print help
  -V, --version                    Print version

Examples:
  xmind tree roadmap.xmind --depth 2
  xmind find roadmap.xmind --title "Launch"
  xmind set roadmap.xmind --node path:/Launch --title "Launch plan" --dry-run
  xmind export roadmap.xmind --format markdown --output roadmap.md
